At least five people are missing after a cargo ship caught fire at the port of Qingdao. The cause remains unclear.

At least 25 people were killed and five remain missing after a fire on a cargo vessel receiving repairs at a shipyard in the northeastern Chinese port city of Qingdao, state media reported on Thursday.&#160;

State broadcaster CCTV reported the vessel with 42 people on board caught fire at around 11:15 a.m. local time, and were extinguished around&#160;2:30 p.m.&#160;(0630 UTC)."

The ship was identified as the 190-metre (623-foot) long bulk carrier "Ocean Melody,"&#160;which sails under a Liberian flag, state news agency Xinhua reported.&#160;

Chinese&#160;President Xi Jinping issued has "important instructions" to conduct a search and rescue mission, while also calling for an investigation into anyone who could be&#160;responsible for the incident, Xinhua added.&#160;

Xi said that "all regions and relevant departments must draw profound lessons from this incident, thoroughly investigate and rectify all types of fire hazards".

The vessel was undergoing repairs&#160;at Qingdao's&#160;Beihai Shipbuilding Co, part of the&#160; China State Shipbuilding Corporation (CSSC), one of the world's largest shipbuilders.

